{
  "titre": "Exprimer le but",
  "titreSurligne": "but",
  "accroche": "Pour quoi faire&nbsp;? To, so that.",
  "bonus": "**to** + base · **in order to / so as to** · **so that** + proposition",
  "illustration": {
    "fichier": "assets-sources/fiches/illustrations/5e/anglais/exprimer-le-but.webp",
    "prompt": "a glossy violet archery target with a golden arrow in the center, tiny golden sparkles, same art style as the reference icons, magenta background"
  },
  "marcel": "Pour y arriver,\nto + verbe&nbsp;!",
  "rangs": [
    {
      "colonnes": "300px 1fr",
      "blocs": [
        {
          "type": "formule",
          "numero": 1,
          "titre": "Le but",
          "lignes": [
            "**to** + base verbale"
          ],
          "petite": true,
          "regle": "Même sujet dans les deux parties → **to**. Sujet différent → **so that**.",
          "note": "jamais for + verbe"
        },
        {
          "type": "tableau",
          "numero": 2,
          "titre": "Les trois constructions",
          "entetes": [
            "Forme",
            "Registre",
            "Exemple"
          ],
          "lignes": [
            [
              "to + base",
              "courant",
              "<i>I went to the shop **to buy** bread.</i>"
            ],
            [
              "in order to / so as to",
              "formel",
              "<i>He left early **in order to** catch the train.</i>"
            ],
            [
              "so that + proposition",
              "autre sujet",
              "<i>I’ll speak slowly **so that** you can understand.</i>"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "blocs": [
        {
          "type": "cartes",
          "numero": 3,
          "titre": "For, deux emplois",
          "colonnes": 3,
          "cartes": [
            {
              "titre": "For + nom",
              "texte": "Aller chercher&nbsp;: <i>I went to the shop **for** bread.</i>"
            },
            {
              "titre": "For + -ING",
              "texte": "À quoi sert un objet&nbsp;: <i>This knife is **for cutting** bread.</i>"
            },
            {
              "titre": "But négatif",
              "texte": "<i>I wrote it down **so as not to** forget.</i> (aussi <i>in order not to</i>)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "blocs": [
        {
          "type": "verdicts",
          "numero": 4,
          "titre": "Le but d’une action",
          "oui": {
            "titre": "To + base verbale",
            "texte": "<i>I went to the shop **to buy** bread.</i>"
          },
          "non": {
            "titre": "For + verbe",
            "texte": "<i>I went to the shop **for buying** bread.</i>"
          },
          "essai": {
            "titre": "Essai",
            "texte": "<i>She saved money ___ her son could study abroad.</i> → **so that**&nbsp;: un autre sujet."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "blocs": [
        {
          "type": "etapes",
          "numero": 5,
          "titre": "La méthode",
          "etapes": [
            {
              "titre": "Même sujet&nbsp;?",
              "texte": "Oui → <i>to</i> (ou <i>in order to</i>)."
            },
            {
              "titre": "Autre sujet&nbsp;?",
              "texte": "Phrase complète avec **so that**."
            },
            {
              "titre": "Un modal",
              "texte": "Après <i>so that</i> : souvent <i>can, could, will, would</i>."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "blocs": [
        {
          "type": "texte",
          "numero": "★",
          "titre": "À retenir",
          "paragraphes": [
            "Pour dire **pourquoi** on fait quelque chose, l’anglais emploie **to + verbe**. Jamais <i>for</i> suivi d’un verbe conjugué ou en <i>-ing</i> pour un but."
          ],
          "teinte": "jaune"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "colonnes": "1fr 1fr",
      "blocs": [
        {
          "type": "liste",
          "numero": 6,
          "titre": "Interroger sur le but",
          "deux": true,
          "items": [
            {
              "titre": "What… for?",
              "texte": "<i>What did you do that **for**?</i>"
            },
            {
              "titre": "Why?",
              "texte": "<i>Why did you call? — **To** ask you something.</i>"
            },
            {
              "titre": "Négatif",
              "texte": "<i>so as not to</i>, <i>in order not to</i>"
            },
            {
              "titre": "Courant",
              "texte": "<i>to</i> suffit dans la plupart des cas"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "pieges",
          "items": [
            "<i>for buying bread</i> → <i>**to buy** bread</i>",
            "<i>I speak slowly for you understand</i> → <i>**so that** you understand</i>",
            "<i>to bread</i> → <i>**for** bread</i> (avec un nom).",
            "Autre sujet : <i>to</i> seul ne marche pas, il faut **so that**."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "blocs": [
        {
          "type": "test",
          "questions": [
            "<i>I went to the shop ___ buy bread.</i>",
            "<i>I speak slowly ___ you can understand.</i>",
            "<i>This knife is ___ cutting bread.</i>"
          ],
          "reponses": "1) to 2) so that 3) for"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
